        <mxCell id="bdm-t_note" value="&lt;b&gt;Why plain Postgres&lt;/b&gt;: relational + pgvector (HNSW) + tsvector + graph as adjacency tables queried with recursive CTEs (depth ≤ 2). One transaction covers a fact, its entities, its embedding and its outbox event: no second store to drift out of sync. Apache AGE (openCypher) is an optional upgrade if graph queries outgrow CTEs. memories is hash-partitioned by tenant (16), recall_log by month." style="shape=note;size=14;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#FFFBEB;strokeColor=#D6B656;fontColor=#1E293B;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;spacingRight=8;shadow=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="bdm-er">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="730" width="1460" height="110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
